From: alvesmaicon <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: sun4i-lradc-keys - honor the autorepeat property

The GA36-MB device trees set "autorepeat" on the lradc node, the way
adc-keys and gpio-keys read it, but this driver never looked at it:
EV_REP was never set and a held key sent a single press. Set EV_REP when
the node has the property, as adc-keys does.

The input core's default when EV_REP is set is a 250 ms delay, then a
repeat every 33 ms. On volume keys that takes the level from 0 to 100%
in under a second, so use 400 ms and 120 ms.

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c b/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/sun4i-lradc-keys.c
@@ -301,6 +301,12 @@
 	__set_bit(EV_KEY, lradc->input->evbit);
 	for (i = 0; i < lradc->chan0_map_count; i++)
 		__set_bit(lradc->chan0_map[i].keycode, lradc->input->keybit);
+
+	if (device_property_read_bool(dev, "autorepeat")) {
+		__set_bit(EV_REP, lradc->input->evbit);
+		/* the 250/33 ms default is too fast for volume keys */
+		input_enable_softrepeat(lradc->input, 400, 120);
+	}
 
 	input_set_drvdata(lradc->input, lradc);
 
